gs":[]},"task_tags":["digital_watermarking"],"contribution_type":"survey","review_status":"verified","doi":"10.1109/ojcs.2026.3651292","arxiv_id":"","openalex_id":"","semantic_scholar_id":"","primary_url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/ojcs.2026.3651292","citation_count":0,"provenance":[{"source":"crossref","source_id":"10.1109/ojcs.2026.3651292","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/ojcs.2026.3651292","query":"deep learning image watermarking","retrieved_at":"2026-07-16T04:06:13Z"}],"notes":"快速批量核验：具有稳定来源，且任务标签与图像取证范围一致。"},{"id":"paper-1c95a65c63674014","title":"NSFF: Noise and semantic features fusion for AI-generated image detection","title_zh":"","year":2026,"publication_date":"","abstract":"Advanced generative models are capable of producing photorealistic images with strong semantic consistency and a high degree of controllability. Such images are highly convincing in real-world scenarios and may facilitate the malicious spread and misuse of misinformation. Therefore, it is urgently needed to develop reliable detectors to identify AI-generated images. However, previous methods have generally relied on large-scale training sets composed of real and generated images, which not only lead to lengthy training processes but also often suffer from significant performance degradation when detecting images produced by unknown generative models. To address this issue, we propose a general detection framework for AI-generated images, termed NSFF. Unlike previous methods that primarily combined texture features and semantic information, NSFF explicitly utilizes noise artifacts in poorly textured regions and combines global and local semantic information to obtain more complementary and robust representations. We extracted an equal number of real and AI-generated images from four benchmark datasets to construct the testing set. The experiments show that NSFF can effectively generalize to images generated by previously unseen models with only 2000 images for small-scale supervised training. In the test set, our method achieved an average accuracy of 80.82%. Our code can be found at https://github.com/IMUT-YangHr/NSFF-main.","authors":[{"id":"author-a77d78f906b0de","name":"Haoran Yang","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"author-d00aabdfc02ede","name":"Ruiqiang Ma","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"author-52a4db9d00555a","name":"Gang Wang","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"author-981ead90103cdd","name":"Jien Kato","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]}],"institution_ids":[],"venue":{"id":"venue-db868e88e49fe0","name":"Neural Networks","short_name":"NN","type":"journal","issn":"","rankings":[{"system":"CAS","level":"2","category":"计算机科学","scope":"大类","is_top":true,"version":"2025","source_url":"https://www.iikx.com/sci/technology/37754.html","verified_at":"2026-08-12"},{"system":"JCR","level":"Q1","category":"Computer Science; Neurosciences","scope":"","is_top":false,"version":"2026","source_url":"https://www.iikx.com/sci/technology/37754.html","verified_at":"2026-08-12"}]},"task_tags":["synthetic_detection"],"contribution_type":"method","review_status":"verified","doi":"10.1016/j.neunet.2026.109130","arxiv_id":"","openalex_id":"W7161630969","semantic_scholar_id":"","primary_url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.neunet.2026.109130","citation_count":0,"provenance":[{"source":"authorized_seed","source_id":"curated:167b4dd09fa505470bce","url":"https://openalex.org/W7161630969","query":"","retrieved_at":"2026-07-15T00:00:00Z"},{"source":"crossref","source_id":"10.1016/j.neunet.2026.109130","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.neunet.2026.109130","query":"AI generated image detection","retrieved_at":"2026-07-15T06:17:01Z"},{"source":"dblp","source_id":"journals/nn/YangMWK26","url":"https://dblp.org/rec/journals/nn/YangMWK26","query":"AI generated image detection","retrieved_at":"2026-07-15T06:20:35Z"},{"source":"semantic_scholar","source_id":"8d0b52bbe7943433803df8e34eaf3b2a4d461960","url":"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/8d0b52bbe7943433803df8e34eaf3b2a4d461960","query":"AI generated image detector robustness","retrieved_at":"2026-07-16T04:10:16Z"}],"notes":""},{"id":"paper-851861806bf93214","title":"Steganalysis of neural networks using implicit features","title_zh":"","year":2026,"publication_date":"","abstract":"Deep neural networks are used increasingly in daily life. Many models contain redundant parameters that render them susceptible to being exploited for transmitting secret data, thereby injecting malware or stealing sensitive data. Research on steganographic schemes for neural networks is therefore necessary. Existing steganalysis methods often require access to network parameters, while black-box approaches achieve limited accuracy. In this work, we propose a black-box steganalysis scheme that feeds a fixed sequence of images into the target network to extract implicit features, which are then used to train a steganalysis network. This is a black-box steganalysis framework without access to internal network parameter, leveraging output probabilities from fixed image sequences to capture model behavior and enabling steganography detection across diverse network architectures. Experiments show that our method improves accuracy by 6–39.65% compared to existing steganalysis schemes.","authors":[{"id":"2180628258","name":"Jiaming Cao","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"a5004865399","name":"Zichi Wang","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"2214383767","name":"Yunlong Hao","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"2277147819","name":"Xinpeng Zhang","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]}],"institution_ids":[],"venue":{"id":"venue-78fd5cac8c025b","name":"Cybersecurity","short_name":"","type":"unknown","issn":"","rankings":[]},"task_tags":["image_steganalysis"],"contribution_type":"analysis","review_status":"verified","doi":"10.1186/s42400-025-00519-6","arxiv_id":"","openalex_id":"","semantic_scholar_id":"1231a027c686ab384b73d733bcac267d0457637b","primary_url":"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/1231a027c686ab384b73d733bcac267d0457637b","citation_count":0,"provenance":[{"source":"semantic_scholar","source_id":"1231a027c686ab384b73d733bcac267d0457637b","url":"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/1231a027c686ab384b73d733bcac267d0457637b","query":"image steganalysis detection","retrieved_at":"2026-07-16T04:09:45Z"}],"notes":"快速批量核验：具有稳定来源，且任务标签与图像取证范围一致。"},{"id":"paper-822480145c77f614","title":"Text-aware CLIP: A Generalized Method for Deepfake and Fake News Detection","title_zh":"","year":2026,"publication_date":"","abstract":"","authors":[{"id":"author-cff4384d90ab6b","name":"Shouxin Liu","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"author-38354b5bffa064","name":"Yihang Wang","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"author-92dbc3ebb6e10a","name":"Junfeng Guo","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"author-99c4aa649fe406","name":"Hongran Zeng","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"author-3cc7f55f18a902","name":"In-Kwon Lee","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"a5085698418","name":"Yushu Zhang","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"author-445ff4dfb35191","name":"Xiaowei Li","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]}],"institution_ids":[],"venue":{"id":"venue-057a3fc9c53ec6","name":"IEEE Transactions on Multimedia","short_name":"TMM","type":"journal","issn":"1520-9210","rankings":[{"system":"CAS","level":"1","category":"计算机科学","scope":"大类","is_top":true,"version":"2025","source_url":"https://www.iikx.com/sci/technology/13038.html","verified_at":"2026-08-12"},{"system":"JCR","level":"Q1","category":"Computer Science; Telecommunications","scope":"","is_top":false,"version":"2026","source_url":"https://www.iikx.com/sci/technology/13038.html","verified_at":"2026-08-12"}]},"task_tags":["deepfake_detection"],"contribution_type":"method","review_status":"verified","doi":"10.1109/tmm.2026.3682152","arxiv_id":"","openalex_id":"","semantic_scholar_id":"","primary_url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/tmm.2026.3682152","citation_count":0,"provenance":[{"source":"crossref","source_id":"10.1109/tmm.2026.3682152","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/tmm.2026.3682152","query":"deepfake image detection IEEE Transactions on Multimedia","retrieved_at":"2026-07-16T04:08:06Z"}],"notes":"快速批量核验：具有稳定来源，且任务标签与图像取证范围一致。"},{"id":"paper-82a68e20ddc8f814","title":"IMAGE RECOGNITION CHATBOT USING GENERATIVE AI","title_zh":"","year":2025,"publication_date":"","abstract":"","authors":[],"institution_ids":[],"venue":{"id":"venue-1c0bed34ef4079","name":"International Research Journal of Modernization in Engineering Technology &amp; Science","short_name":"","type":"journal","issn":"2582-5208","rankings":[]},"task_tags":["image_forgery"],"contribution_type":"method","review_status":"verified","doi":"10.56726/irjmets82955","arxiv_id":"","openalex_id":"","semantic_scholar_id":"","primary_url":"https://doi.org/10.56726/irjmets82955","citation_count":0,"provenance":[{"source":"crossref","source_id":"10.56726/irjmets82955","url":"https://doi.org/10.56726/irjmets82955","query":"fake image detection generative AI","retrieved_at":"2026-07-16T07:30:02Z"}],"notes":"快速批量核验：具有稳定来源，且任务标签与图像取证范围一致。"},{"id":"paper-5559d7e1df239a14","title":"LDR-Net: A Novel Framework for AI-generated Image Detection via Localized Discrepancy Representation","title_zh":"","year":2025,"publication_date":"","abstract":"With the rapid advancement of generative models, the visual quality of generated images has become nearly indistinguishable from the real ones, posing challenges to content authenticity verification. Existing methods for detecting AI-generated images primarily focus on specific forgery clues, which are often tailored to particular generative models like GANs or diffusion models. These approaches struggle to generalize across architectures. Building on the observation that generative images often exhibit local anomalies, such as excessive smoothness, blurred textures, and unnatural pixel variations in small regions, we propose the localized discrepancy representation network (LDR-Net), a novel approach for detecting AI-generated images. LDR-Net captures smoothing artifacts and texture irregularities, which are common but often overlooked. It integrates two complementary modules: local gradient autocorrelation (LGA) which models local smoothing anomalies to detect smoothing anomalies, and local variation pattern (LVP) which captures unnatural regularities by modeling the complexity of image patterns. By merging LGA and LVP features, a comprehensive representation of localized discrepancies can be provided. Extensive experiments demonstrate that our LDR-Net achieves state-of-the-art performance in detecting generated images and exhibits satisfactory generalization across unseen generative models. The code will be released upon acceptance of this paper.","authors":[{"id":"a5100360559","name":"Jiaxin Chen","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"2342471131","name":"Miao Hu","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"a5085673014","name":"Dengyong Zhang","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"2342098244","name":"Yun Song","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"a5100716299","name":"Xin Liao","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]}],"institution_ids":[],"venue":{"id":"venue-886c3c4a4b4e64","name":"arXiv.org","short_name":"","type":"unknown","issn":"","rankings":[]},"task_tags":["synthetic_detection"],"contribution_type":"method","review_status":"verified","doi":"10.48550/arxiv.2501.13475","arxiv_id":"2501.13475","openalex_id":"","semantic_scholar_id":"47a0acf49a84fc96b760f66d8e9c48723928b95d","primary_url":"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/47a0acf49a84fc96b760f66d8e9c48723928b95d","citation_count":2,"provenance":[{"source":"semantic_scholar","source_id":"47a0acf49a84fc96b760f66d8e9c48723928b95d","url":"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/47a0acf49a84fc96b760f66d8e9c48723928b95d","query":"generalizable AI generated image detection","retrieved_at":"2026-07-15T18:40:02Z"}],"notes":"快速批量核验：已有稳定来源，且现有任务标签与图像取证范围一致。"},{"id":"paper-4d6ecff3c7808214","title":"Multi-Domain Information