:"","type":"unknown","issn":"1865-0929","rankings":[]},"task_tags":["image_forgery"],"contribution_type":"method","review_status":"verified","doi":"10.1007/978-3-031-31407-0_20","arxiv_id":"","openalex_id":"","semantic_scholar_id":"","primary_url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-031-31407-0_20","citation_count":1,"provenance":[{"source":"crossref","source_id":"10.1007/978-3-031-31407-0_20","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-031-31407-0_20","query":"image splicing detection","retrieved_at":"2026-07-16T07:30:44Z"}],"notes":"快速批量核验：具有稳定来源，且任务标签与图像取证范围一致。"},{"id":"paper-8795d4f718878b14","title":"A new face image manipulation reveal scheme based on face detection and image watermarking","title_zh":"","year":2022,"publication_date":"2022-09-13","abstract":"Face image manipulation (FIM) algorithms and applications are increasing and distributing rapidly. Nowadays, one can easily find an application to manipulate face images for different purposes. After the development and popularity of “DeepFakes”, the research community highlighted the necessity of implementing new detection techniques that can reveal FIM. The available FIM detection techniques have different limitations and most of the presented schemes require a prior knowledge of the FIM method that has been applied to generate the manipulated face image which makes them restricted. In this paper, we present a new face image manipulation reveal (FIMR) scheme based on face detection algorithm and image watermarking technique in the transform domain. The proposed scheme does not need a prior knowledge of the FIM method thus it can reveal different types of FIM. Experiments have been conducted to evaluate the performance of the proposed FIMR scheme for face images with different sizes. The results proved that the proposed scheme can successfully reveal different manipulation attacks such as face swap, expression swap, attribute attacks, retouching attacks, and morphing attacks.","authors":[{"id":"a5069604152","name":"Zahraa Aqeel Salih","orcid":"","institution_ids":["i3131779051"]},{"id":"a5086381696","name":"Rasha Thabit","orcid":"0000-0003-4141-5723","institution_ids":["i2801106189"]},{"id":"a5052544534","name":"Khamis A. Zidan","orcid":"0000-0002-3739-7270","institution_ids":["i3131779051"]},{"id":"a5060504389","name":"Bee Ee Khoo","orcid":"0000-0002-3492-2551","institution_ids":["i139322472"]}],"institution_ids":["i139322472","i2801106189","i3131779051"],"venue":{"id":"venue-98aac9a0887bec","name":"2022 IEEE International Conference on Artificial Intelligence in Engineering and Technology (IICAIET)","short_name":"","type":"conference","issn":"","rankings":[]},"task_tags":["content_provenance","deepfake_detection","digital_watermarking","image_forgery"],"contribution_type":"method","review_status":"verified","doi":"10.1109/iicaiet55139.2022.9936838","arxiv_id":"","openalex_id":"W4312963145","semantic_scholar_id":"","primary_url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/iicaiet55139.2022.9936838","citation_count":8,"provenance":[{"source":"openalex","source_id":"W4312963145","url":"https://openalex.org/W4312963145","query":"face manipulation detection","retrieved_at":"2026-07-15T06:11:49Z"},{"source":"crossref","source_id":"10.1109/iicaiet55139.2022.9936838","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/iicaiet55139.2022.9936838","query":"face manipulation detection","retrieved_at":"2026-07-16T04:05:30Z"}],"notes":"快速批量核验：已有稳定来源，且现有任务标签与图像取证范围一致。"},{"id":"paper-29f202478e047214","title":"Detecting Adversarial Examples Using Rich Residual Models to Improve Data Security in CNN Models","title_zh":"","year":2022,"publication_date":"","abstract":"The convolution neural network (CNN) is vulnerable to the adversarial attack, because the attack can generate adversarial images to force the CNN to misclassify the original label of the clean image. To defend against the adversarial attack, we propose to detect the adversarial images first and then prevent feeding the adversarial image into the CNN model. In this paper, we employ a steganalysis based method based on rich residual models to detect adversarial images which are generated by the typical attacks including BIM and DEEPFOOL. The rich residual models not only reduce the influences from natural image contents, but also enhance the diversity of the feature. Two typical and complementary methods spatial rich model (SRM) and projected spatial rich model (PSRM) are used to extract the feature, where SRM finely capture the statistical changes on co-occurrence in a small neighborhood, and PSRM remedy the loss information caused by SRM. Experimental results on CIFAR-IO and ImageNet show that the proposed method obtained better performance than existing steganalysis methods for detecting adversarial images generated by BIM and DEEPFOOL attack. The research results are expected to improve the recognition ability of image adversarial samples in the convolutional neural network model, and support the data security of natural image content in image recognition.","authors":[{"id":"2115598664","name":"Kaijun Wu","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"2064522683","name":"Bo Tian","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"2307763129","name":"You-wei Wen","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"2108226264","name":"Xue Wang","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]}],"institution_ids":[],"venue":{"id":"venue-ef0403ec616c7f","name":"2022 7th International Conference on Communication, Image and Signal Processing (CCISP)","short_name":"","type":"unknown","issn":"","rankings":[]},"task_tags":["image_steganalysis"],"contribution_type":"method","review_status":"verified","doi":"10.1109/ccisp55629.2022.9974244","arxiv_id":"","openalex_id":"","semantic_scholar_id":"9ed0e39a3dd1d53d06ed8641a2851bc0d97d70e5","primary_url":"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/9ed0e39a3dd1d53d06ed8641a2851bc0d97d70e5","citation_count":1,"provenance":[{"source":"semantic_scholar","source_id":"9ed0e39a3dd1d53d06ed8641a2851bc0d97d70e5","url":"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/9ed0e39a3dd1d53d06ed8641a2851bc0d97d70e5","query":"rich model image steganalysis","retrieved_at":"2026-07-16T04:11:06Z"}],"notes":"快速批量核验：具有稳定来源，且任务标签与图像取证范围一致。"},{"id":"paper-9fb28518be0ea014","title":"Robust color image watermarking using multiple fractional-order moments and chaotic map","title_zh":"","year":2022,"publication_date":"","abstract":"","authors":[{"id":"a5074599271","name":"Khalid M. Hosny","orcid":"0000-0001-8065-8977","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"author-16d699e27f47b2","name":"Mohamed M. Darwish","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]}],"institution_ids":[],"venue":{"id":"venue-e43d0ed7069ca7","name":"Multimedia Tools and Applications","short_name":"MTAP","type":"journal","issn":"1380-7501","rankings":[]},"task_tags":["digital_watermarking"],"contribution_type":"method","review_status":"verified","doi":"10.1007/s11042-022-12282-8","arxiv_id":"","openalex_id":"","semantic_scholar_id":"","primary_url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s11042-022-12282-8","citation_count":21,"provenance":[{"source":"crossref","source_id":"10.1007/s11042-022-12282-8","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s11042-022-12282-8","query":"image watermarking @ ACM Multimedia","retrieved_at":"2026-07-16T07:42:52Z"}],"notes":"快速批量核验：具有稳定来源，且任务标签与图像取证范围一致。"},{"id":"paper-eb14a291353aa014","title":"Image forgery detection using Deep Neural Network","title_zh":"","year":2021,"publication_date":"2021-08-26","abstract":"Due to the availability of deep networks, progress has been made in the field of image recognition. Images and videos are spreading very conveniently and with the availability of strong editing tools the tampering of digital content become easy. To detect such scams, we proposed techniques. In our paper, we proposed two important aspects of employing deep convolutional neural networks to image forgery detection. We first explore and examine different pre-processing method along with convolutional neural networks (CNN) architecture. Later we evaluated the different transfer learning for pre-trained ImageNet(via-fine-tuning) and implement it over our dataset CASIA V2.0. So, it covers the pre-processing techniques with basic CNN model and later see the powerful effect of the transfer learning models.","authors":[{"id":"a5101731414","name":"Anushka Singh","orcid":"0009-0003-0274-808X","institution_ids":["i36090812"]},{"id":"a5114888365","name":"Jyotsna Singh","orcid":"0000-0003-4437-4680","institution_ids":["i36090812"]}],"institution_ids":["i36090812"],"venue":null,"task_tags":["image_forgery"],"contribution_type":"method","review_status":"verified","doi":"10.1109/spin52536.2021.9565953","arxiv_id":"","openalex_id":"W3211032589","semantic_scholar_id":"","primary_url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/spin52536.2021.9565953","citation_count":21,"provenance":[{"source":"openalex","source_id":"W3211032589","url":"https://openalex.org/W3211032589","query":"image forgery detection","retrieved_at":"2026-07-15T06:11:49Z"},{"source":"crossref","source_id":"10.1109/spin52536.2021.9565953","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/spin52536.2021.9565953","query":"image forgery detection","retrieved_at":"2026-07-16T07:32:03Z"}],"notes":"快速批量核验：已有稳定来源，且现有任务标签与图像取证范围一致。"},{"id":"paper-e876451f10767014","title":"Image steganography using genetic algorithm for cover image selection and embedding","title_zh":"","year":2021,"publication_date":"","abstract":"Abstract Data interchange through internet becomes an eminent technique and hence data security has become a big challenge in the field of communication with the increased use of internet. Demand for data authentication and effective means to control data integrity has been steadily increasing. Such a demand is due to the ease with which digital data can be tampered. Thus, cryptography and watermarking can be replaced with steganography for secure data communication and data privacy. In this paper, the carrier image is selected such that the payload/secret image and least significant bits of carrier image are matched with larger degree of compatibility and the hiding process introduces negligible changes in the resulted stego image based on genetic algorithm. In the proposed method we have achieved 30 to 40% improvements in the performance when compared to different existing methods. Selection of a suitable cover image and hiding the secret data to enhance the imperceptibility is a very challenging task. Genetic algorithm is used to ease the work of exploring an impossible task of selection from the trillions and millions of combinations.","authors":[{"id":"113936013","name":"M. Shyla","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"2110670489","name":"K. Kumar","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"1576453694","name":"Rajendra Kumar Das","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]}],"institution_ids":[],"venue":{"id":"venue-71208f9bf94eff","name":"Soft Computing Letters","short_name":"","type":"unknown","issn":"","rankings":[]},"task_tags":["image_steganalysis"],"contribution_type":"method","review_status":"verified","doi":"10.1016/j.socl.2021.100021","arxiv_id":"","openalex_id":"","semantic_scholar_id":"09371c95117bc335b141ea2f3abae1a4efc05f93","primary_url":"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/09371c95117bc335b141ea2f3abae1a4efc05f93","citation_count":23,"provenance":[{"source":"semantic_scholar","source_id":"09371c95117bc335b141ea2f3abae1a4efc05f93","url":"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/09371c95117bc335b141ea2f3abae1a4efc05f93","query":"digital image watermarking authentication","retrieved_at":"2026-07-16T04:09:53Z"}],"notes":"快速批量核验：具有稳定来源，且任务标签与图像取证范围一致。"},{"id":"paper-cd96d9905c1fe414","title":"Image Splicing Detection using Uniform Local Binary Pattern and Wavelet Transform","title_zh":"","year":2019,"publication_date":"2019-10-29","abstract":"","authors":[{"id":"a5025923277","name":"Eman I. Abd El-Latif","orcid":"","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"a5071123879","name":"Ahmed Taha","orcid":"0000-0002-4214-9247","institution_ids":[]},{"id":"a5044492187","name":"Hala H. Zayed","orcid":"0000-0001-6779-7577","institution_ids":[]}],"institution_ids":[],"venue":{"id":"venue-b4fb285cfef928","name":"Journal of Engineering and Applied Sciences","short_name":"","type":"journal","issn":"","rankings":[]},"task_tags":["image_forgery"],"contribution_type":"method","review_status":"verified","doi":"10.36478/jeasci.2019.7679.7684","arxiv_id":"","openalex_id":"W2982339378","semantic_scholar_id":"","primary_url":"https://doi.org/10.36478/jeasci.2019.7679.7684","citation_count":4,"provenance":[{"source":"openalex","source_id":"W2982339378","url":"https://openalex.org/W2982339378","query":"image splicing detection","retrieved_at":"2026-07-15T06:11:49Z"},{"source":"crossref","source_id":"10.36478/jeasci.2019.7679.7684","url":"https://doi.org/10.36478/jeasci.2019.7679.7684","query":"image splicing detection","retrieved_at":"2026-07-16T07:30:44Z"}],"notes":"快速批量核验：已有稳定来源，且现有任务标签与图像取证范围一致。"},{"id":"paper-4bb51a56023d4514","title":"A Channel-Dependent Statistical Watermark Detector for Color Images","title_zh":"","year":2018,"publication_date":"2018-06-29","abstract":"Data security is a main concern in everyday data transmissions over the Internet. A possible solution to guarantee secure and legitimate transaction is via hiding a piece of tractable information into the multimedia signal, that is, watermarking. In this paper, we propose a new color image watermarking scheme and its corresponding detector in the sparse domain. The watermark detector aims at verifying the ownership and circumventing any unauthorized duplication of the digital data. Most of the existing color image watermarking schemes disregard the inter-channel dependencies. In view of this, we take into account the interchannel dependencies between RGB channels and interscale dependencies of the sparse coefficients of color images by employing the hidden Markov model. An efficient detector is designed by establishing a binary hypothesis test through which the existence of the hidden watermark is examined. Experiments are conducted to evaluate the performance of the proposed watermark detector for color images. The results show that the proposed detector provides detection rates higher than those provided by the other detectors, even in the presence of attacks. It is also shown that the proposed detector exhibits better performance in terms of the robustness of the embedded watermark.","authors":[{"id":"a5029996071","name":"Marzieh Amini","orcid":"0000-0002-5217-2969","institution_ids":["i60158472"]},{"id":"a5072288399","name":"Hamidreza Sadreazami","orcid":"0000-0002-2624-0681","institution_ids":["i60158472"]},{"id":"a5068820891","name":"M. Omair Ahmad","orcid":"0000-0002-2924-6659","institution_ids":["i60158472"]},{"id":"a5013967994","name":"M.N.S. Swamy","orcid":"0000-0002-3989-5476","institution_ids":["i60158472"]}],"institution_ids":["i60158472"],"venue":{"id":"venue-057a3fc9c53ec6","name":"IEEE Transactions on Multimedia","short_name":"TMM","type":"journal","issn":"","rankings":[{"system":"CAS","level":"1","category":"计算机科学","scope":"大类","is_top":true,"version":"2025","source_url":"https://www.iikx.com/sci/technology/13038.html","verified_at":"2026-08-12"},{"system":"JCR","level":"Q1","category":"Computer Science; Telecommunications","scope":"","is_top":false,"version":"2026","source_url":"https://www.iikx.com/sci/technology/13038.html","verified_at":"2026-08-12"}]},"task_tags":["digital_watermarking"],"contribution_type":"method","review_status":"verified","doi":"10.1109/tmm.2018.2851447","arxiv_id":"","openalex_id":"W2811207102","semantic_scholar_id":"","primary_url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/tmm.2018.2851447","citation_count":56,"provenance":[{"source":"openalex","source_id":"W2811207102","url":"https://openalex.org/W2811207102","query":"image watermark detection robustness","retrieved_at":"2026-07-15T06:11:49Z"}],"notes":"快速批量核验：已有稳定来源，且现有任务标签与图像取证范围一致。"},{"id":"paper-1de9590842e26a14","title":"Performance analysis of image steganalysis techniques and future research direct